{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PinRobustnessOfRatios","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PinRobustnessOfRatios","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.LogDeriv","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hbarInvSq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hbarInvSq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PinRobustnessOfRatios.lean#L87-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hbarInvSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.hbarInvSq","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PinRobustnessOfRatios.lean#L82-L85","doc":"The absolute muon anchor's `ℏ_q⁻²` factor, `(q/(q−1))²` (`= 1/ℏ_q²`, `ℏ_q = (q−1)/q`). It is the\nsole carrier of the large pin-sensitivity `S = 2/(q−1)`. On the substrate ray `q > 1` it is a\nstrictly positive unit — the hypothesis the pin-robustness lemmas require. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.logDeriv_pure_anchor_ratio_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.logDeriv_pure_anchor_ratio_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PinRobustnessOfRatios.lean#L68-L80","doc":"**A ratio of two pure-anchor observables is pin-CONSTANT.** If `f = c₁·anchor` and\n`g = c₂·anchor` (both proportional to the same anchor — e.g. two `ℏ_q⁻²`-masses), the ratio has zero\nlogarithmic derivative everywhere the anchor is a unit: perfect pin-robustness. The μ–p tension, which\nlives in `anchor` itself, is invisible in any such ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.logDeriv_ratio_indep_of_shared_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.logDeriv_ratio_indep_of_shared_factor","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PinRobustnessOfRatios.lean#L59-L66","doc":"**Pin-sensitivity of a ratio is anchor-independent.** The logarithmic derivative of the ratio\n`(h·a)/(h·b)` equals that of `a/b`: the shared factor `h` — e.g. the absolute anchor `ℏ_q⁻²` — makes\n**zero** contribution to the ratio's pin-sensitivity. This is the generalized Habiro pin-robustness:\n`W_λ` and every mass ratio, sharing the anchor, are blind to it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ratio_shared_factor_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.ratio_shared_factor_eq","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PinRobustnessOfRatios.lean#L51-L57","doc":"**Shared-factor cancellation (pure function identity).** A ratio `(h·a)/(h·b)` equals `a/b`\nwherever the shared factor `h` is nonzero — the anchor cancels. Stated over any field, pointwise. ","signatureChunk":0}]}